# Fractured Identity: "Each player other than its controller creates a token that's a copy of it." In a three-player
# game Bot2's Ornithopter is exiled and both Bot1 (the caster) and Bot3 get a token copy; Bot2, its controller, gets
# none. Turn order is Bot1 (T1, T4), Bot2 (T2), Bot3 (T3); Bot1 casts it on turn 4 with five Moxen.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fractured Identity
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Island
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x17

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fractured Identity.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot3.Battlefield = Ornithopter
